dist/index.js is a single-file esbuild bundle: the whole runtime dependency
tree is inlined into it with no package boundaries, so this list is the only
human-readable inventory of what a consumer executes. An earlier revision named
one package while the bundle in fact carried a full HTTP stack; the entries
below are the resolved runtime tree (`npm ls --omit=dev`) cross-checked against
strings present in the built bundle.

  @4cloudguru/pipeline-task-core        Apache-2.0
  @actions/core                         MIT
  @actions/exec                         MIT
  @actions/http-client                  MIT
  @actions/io                           MIT
  tunnel                                MIT
  undici                                MIT
    includes formdata-polyfill          MIT  (vendored by undici; both banners
    includes ws                         MIT   are reproduced verbatim in the
                                              "Bundled license information"
                                              block at the end of the bundle)

A machine-readable CycloneDX SBOM is generated at release time and attached to
each GitHub Release, alongside a build-provenance attestation over dist/index.js.
